          "The Siliņš catalogue calls Berita the Scandinavian form of Brigita, which it connects with Celtic brigh, “strength”. Behind the Name likewise treats Scandinavian Berit as a variant of Birgit, in the family that includes Latvian Brigita.",
          "The catalogue records Berita in Riga in 1940 (dictionary pages 81; 86). This is an attributed record of use, not proof of the first bearer. The Norwegian rendering manual of 2003 gives Berit as Bērita with a long ē, so it is not used here as a bridge for the short-e spelling."
